## Summary

Implemented PRD-076 (Scope Modularization for Parallel Authoring) in full — a pure file-organization refactor recovering backlog concurrency by splitting the four shared surfaces the scheduler was serializing on.

**1. Config module tree** — `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config.rs` (5164 lines) → `config/` with 15 per-feature files (`providers.rs`, `driver.rs`, `review.rs`, `delivery.rs`, `accounting.rs`, `compression.rs`, `registry_workers.rs`, `daemon.rs`, `inference.rs`, `repository.rs`, `preflight.rs`, `execution.rs`, `artifacts.rs`, `shareable.rs`, `pipeline.rs`), all re-exported from `mod.rs`. Behavior preservation is proven, not asserted: `crates/familiar-ai-core/tests/prd076_config_split_equivalence.rs` resolves the pinned `config/default.toml` fixture and asserts byte-identical JSON against `tests/fixtures/prd076_pinned_effective_config.json`, captured from the pre-split code at HEAD via a throwaway git worktree.

**2. Provider contract split** — `docs/contracts/providers.md` is now a stable index over five domain docs (`providers-inference.md`, `providers-billing.md`, `providers-deploy-targets.md`, `providers-credentials.md`, `providers-registry-migration.md`), with all original content preserved verbatim.

**3. CLI thinning** — Moved the `billing`, `config`, and `worker` subcommand groups (enums + handlers) out of `bin/familiar-ai.rs` into `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/cli/{billing,config,worker}.rs` (2563 → 2037 lines), following the existing `config_cli.rs` pattern. Resolved a naming collision with the daemon's own pre-existing `cli.rs` by relocating it to `cli/daemon_args.rs`. Verified byte-identical `--help` output before/after.

**4. Backlog amendments** — Narrowed `expected_files` in all 11 pending PRDs (038, 053, 058–061, 063, 071–073, 080) plus the completed legacy PRD-032, replacing the four shared surfaces with the specific new files each PRD actually needs.

**5. Execution plan regeneration** — Computed (not estimated) via the real `achievable_width` scheduler function against the amended declarations: the first post-076 round (`038, 053, 058, 080`) has graph width 4, achievable width **2** (>1, satisfying the acceptance criterion). Documented all 7 subsequent rounds, including the honest finding that rounds 4–7 remain width-1 because the four raw-inference adapters (059–063) still share `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/` and `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/` — out of this PRD's declared scope, noted explicitly as a future PRD-059/060/061/063 concern.

**Verification**: full workspace test suite green (65 test binaries, 0 failures), `cargo fmt`/`clippy` clean (only one pre-existing, untouched warning in `bootstrap.rs` and one in `summary_worker.rs`), advisory `metadata-check` exits 0 with no structured-v1 diagnostics.

One deliberate, documented scope boundary: `bin/familiar-ai.rs` is not fully dispatch-only for *all* ~15 CLI domains — only `billing`/`config`/`worker` (the three pending PRDs actually needed) were extracted, matching the Design section's operational success criterion ("pending PRDs extending the CLI declare their module, not the binary"). All other domains (`control`, `backlog`, `drive`, `plan`, `stewardship`, etc.) remain in the binary since no pending PRD touches them and moving them would be unrequested scope expansion.
